      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c9cd29fb-5dd4-56a1-b37a-a524d7b99f8b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Ghost and the Darkness, Bwana Devil, Killers of Kilimanjaro\n- People: Stephen Hopkins, Val Kilmer, Michael Douglas, John Henry Patterson\n- Animals: Tsavo Man-Eaters\n- Places: Tsavo, Kenya, East Africa\n- Projects: Uganda-Mombasa Railway\n\nFacts:\n- In 1898, the Tsavo Man-Eaters attacked and killed workers at Tsavo, Kenya, during the construction of the Uganda-Mombasa Railway in East Africa.\n- The Tsavo Man-Eaters were notable for unusual behavior, including the number of men they killed and the manner of their attacks.\n- John Henry Patterson's book inspired the Hollywood films Bwana Devil (1952), Killers of Kilimanjaro (1959), and The Ghost and the Darkness (1996).\n- The Ghost and the Darkness is a 1996 American historical adventure film directed by Stephen Hopkins and starring Val Kilmer and Michael Douglas.\n- The Ghost and the Darkness presents a fictionalized account of the Tsavo Man-Eaters, and Val Kilmer portrayed John Henry Patterson in the film.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "39417242-99ea-5f2b-ac33-153194962bf1",
        "text": "Page: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The Ghost and the Darkness is a 1996 American historical adventure film directed by Stephen Hopkins and starring Val Kilmer and Michael Douglas.\nPage: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The story is a fictionalized account of the Tsavo Man-Eaters, two lions that attacked and killed workers at Tsavo, Kenya, during the building of the Uganda-Mombasa Railway in East Africa in 1898.\nPage: Tsavo Man-Eaters. Sentence: The significance of this pair of lions was their unusual behavior, such as the number of men killed and the manner of the attacks.\nPage: John Henry Patterson (author). Sentence: The book has inspired three Hollywood films - \"Bwana Devil\" (1952), \"Killers of Kilimanjaro\" (1959) and \"The Ghost and the Darkness\" (1996) in which he was portrayed by Val Kilmer.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
